.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-mr-create 1  "swarm 0.2.1" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-mr\-create \- Propose a branch; run it again to add your new commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm mr create\fR [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBRANCH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Propose a branch; run it again to add your new commits
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch to merge into (default: the repo\*(Aqs default branch)
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
A repo ID or link; by default the swarm remote of this clone
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Use what is already here instead of syncing first
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Title (default: taken from the commits)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
Description
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIBRANCH\fR]
Branch to propose (default: the current one)
